                     /note="sigma factors are initiation factors that promote
                     the attachment of RNA polymerase to specific initiation
                     sites and are then released; sigma 54 factor is responsible
                     for the expression of enzymes involved in nitrogen
                     assimilation and metabolism; the rhizobia often have 2
                     copies of this sigma factor; in Rhizobium etli RpoN1 shown
                     to be involved in the assimilation of several nitrogen and
                     carbon sources during free-living aerobic growth and RpoN2
                     is involved in symbiotic nitrogen fixation; in
                     Bradyrhizobium both RpoN1 and N2 are functional in
                     free-living and symbiotic conditions, rpoN1 gene was
                     regulated in response to oxygen; Derived by automated
                     computational analysis using gene prediction method:
                     Protein Homology."
