                     /note="functions in protein export; can interact with
                     acidic membrane phospholipids and the SecYEG protein
                     complex; binds to preproteins; binds to ATP and undergoes a
                     conformational change to promote membrane insertion of
                     SecA/bound preprotein; ATP hydrolysis appears to drive
                     release of the preprotein from SecA and deinsertion of SecA
                     from the membrane; additional proteins SecD/F/YajC aid SecA
                     recycling; exists in an equilibrium between monomers and
                     dimers; may possibly form higher order oligomers; proteins
                     in this cluster correspond SecA1; SecA2 is not essential
                     and seems to play a role in secretion of a subset of
                     proteins; Derived by automated computational analysis using
                     gene prediction method: Protein Homology."
