                     conditions; forms two stacked rings of heptamers to form a
                     barrel-shaped 14mer; ends can be capped by GroES; misfolded
                     proteins enter the barrel where they are refolded when
                     GroES binds; many bacteria have multiple copies of the
                     groEL gene which are active under different environmental
                     conditions; the B.japonicum protein in this cluster is
                     expressed constitutively; in Rhodobacter, Corynebacterium
                     and Rhizobium this protein is essential for growth; Derived
                     by automated computational analysis using gene prediction
