                     /note="10 kDa chaperonin; Cpn10; GroES; forms
                     homoheptameric ring; binds to one or both ends of the GroEL
                     double barrel in the presence of adenine nucleotides
                     capping it; folding of unfolded substrates initiates in a
                     GroEL-substrate bound and capped by GroES; release of the
                     folded substrate is dependent on ATP binding and hydrolysis
                     in the trans ring; Derived by automated computational
                     analysis using gene prediction method: Protein Homology."
